From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:55:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] glm5_next/cuda: a resumed shared prefix copies its rows into
 free rows, TF_GLM_SHARED_PREFIX_COPY (MiaAI-Lab recipe patch 0071)

A request that resumes a shared system prompt's kept state took over the extent that held it and evicted every longer
kept state in that extent. The extent belongs to the conversation that first wrote the shared prefix, so another
conversation with the same system prompt (an agent's sub-agent, several chats on one system prompt) deleted that
conversation's state, and its next turn read its whole history again (the recipe's issue #43). MiaAI-Lab's recipe
v1.6 copies the shared rows into an extent of their own when free rows hold it, with patch 0071-glm-shared-prefix-copy;
with no free rows, or with TF_GLM_MULTI_LONE=1, the rows are overwritten as before. Placement only: the same replies.
This ports it behind a switch of this tree's own, off by default:

- multi.py: recipe_switch (a recipe behaviour behind a switch of this tree's own: 0 or unset off, 1 on);
  MultiDecoder.share_copy (TF_GLM_SHARED_PREFIX_COPY); admit's placement is the patch's hunk, gated by the switch.
  The ADMIT's copy path, which both ranks already apply, moves the rows. A longer state is told apart by token ids
  (prompt, c.ids for the recipe's key, c.key): this tree keys no images into kept prompts.
- engine.py: a startup line when the switch is on.
- THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md: "GLM shared-prefix copy".

Unset, admit takes the same path as before (the same evictions in the same order), so replies, kept states, cached
counts and pool rows do not change.

Tests: tests/test_glm_shared_prefix_copy.py (7, CPU): the switch's values; two ranks with free rows, off and on (off:
the sub-agent's resume evicts the writer's own state, and the writer's next turn resumes only the system block; on:
nothing is evicted, and the writer's next turn resumes its whole first turn); with no free rows, and with
TF_GLM_MULTI_LONE=1, the takeover as before; world 1 over the fake AFD wire, off and on. Every reply equals the request
served alone, and both ranks hold the same pools and kept states.

Credit: patch 0071 was written by ezoushen (https://github.com/ezoushen) in
MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold pull request #44 (issue #43), and MiaAI-Lab applied it as
contributed in recipe commit 90d0c8e (v1.6), Apache License 2.0.

Changed from the picked commit: tests/test_glm_shared_prefix_copy.py's world-1 test runs with the host RAM tier
(TF_GLM_KEPT_HOST, TF_GLM_HOST_CACHE_GIB) unset; with the tier, the takeover's eviction parks the writer's state and
its next turn resumes it from host RAM (tests/test_glm_recipe_host_tier.py covers that case).

